WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.440
AWS gets to the same place with accounts,

2
00:00:02.440 --> 00:00:05.626
organizational units and
service control policies,

3
00:00:05.626 --> 00:00:10.550
but GovCloud works differently enough that
you have to plan for it, not discover it.

4
00:00:10.550 --> 00:00:13.658
Accounts are created in pairs
from the commercial side,

5
00:00:13.658 --> 00:00:16.225
and some factory features
simply aren't there.

6
00:00:16.225 --> 00:00:18.475
And GovCloud isn't only for High.

7
00:00:18.475 --> 00:00:23.434
A Moderate system can run there or in
the commercial Regions, and the program's

8
00:00:23.434 --> 00:00:27.850
AWS workloads run in GovCloud, so
check each service, Region by Region.

9
00:00:27.850 --> 00:00:31.087
The other half of this slide
is about your own automation.

10
00:00:31.087 --> 00:00:34.078
A collector calling a
commercial-only API from

11
00:00:34.078 --> 00:00:37.300
inside the boundary is a
crossing nobody approved.

12
00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:41.464
So every adapter declares its
boundary, resolves endpoints from it,

13
00:00:41.464 --> 00:00:44.662
and fails closed when it
doesn't recognize the cloud.

14
00:00:44.662 --> 00:00:46.490
Next, the address plan.
